# The "jarvis" model: a base model with Jarvis's settings and persona built in.
# Build or rebuild it with build-jarvis-model.bat, Settings > AI model > Jarvis model,
# or by hand:   ollama create jarvis -f model\Modelfile
# Your copy is model\Modelfile; updates never overwrite it (this template is tools\jarvis.Modelfile).
#
# To move Jarvis to a stronger base (or later to a fine-tuned GGUF file), change
# only the FROM line and rebuild; the name "jarvis" stays the same everywhere.
#   FROM llama3.2:3b           (about 2 GB, lighter and faster, less capable)
#   FROM ./jarvis-finetuned.gguf
# qwen2.5:7b is about 4.7 GB and fits the 8 GB RTX 4060.
FROM qwen2.5:7b

# Lower than Ollama's default of 0.8, so JSON actions come out well-formed more often.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
# Room for the instructions, long-term memory, document passages and chat history.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# Used when the model is called without its own system message (for example
# "ollama run jarvis"). The Jarvis app sends its own, fuller instructions with
# every chat, and those replace this text.
SYSTEM """You are Jarvis, a personal assistant. Your manner is that of J.A.R.V.I.S. from the Iron Man films: calm, precise and impeccably polite, with dry, understated wit, never gushing and never using exclamation marks or emoji. Address the user as 'sir' unless told otherwise. Write in clean, natural sentences, because your replies may be read aloud. Never claim to have done something you have not done."""
